nce_ids. Read result['content'], not result[:N].\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_file(path: string, content: string, expected_hash: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Replace an editable text file after checking its current hash.\n\n    Args:\n        path: path\n        content: content\n        expected_hash: expected hash\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef read_pdf(start_page: integer, end_page: integer) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Read pages using the repository's read_pdf.py helper. Returns dict: pages (list of {page,text}), evidence_ids, delivery. Extract the required range once; complete pages are sent in bounded batches. Queued ids are not yet read. Do not print all pages.\n\n    Args:\n        start_page: start page\n        end_page: end page\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef run_command(argv: array, cwd: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use '.' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\n\n    Args:\n        argv: argv\n        cwd: cwd\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef update_plan(items: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\n\n    Args:\n        items: List of objects, e.g. [{\"title\":\"Read sources\",\"status\":\"doing\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: array) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\n\n    Args:\n        evidence_ids: evidence ids\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef task_status() -> object:\n    \"\"\"Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef write_note(title: string, content: string, evidence_ids: array, section: string) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence.\n\n    Args:\n        title: Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\n        content: One contiguous string literal, 20..1500 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\n        evidence_ids: Python list[str], e.g. ['ev-abc'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n        section: Required topic: overview/reasoning/tool_use/multi_agent/outlook\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nRead the PDF and update report.json.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"paper\", \"editable\": [\"report.json\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"report.json\"], \"verify_commands\": [], \"required_pages\": [1, 2], \"note_topics\": [\"overview\", \"reasoning\", \"tool_use\", \"multi_agent\", \"outlook\"], \"max_model_calls\": 3}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\nWhen calling write_note, put the complete exact note text in the thought field, then pass that same text as one content string literal in code. This preserves a contiguous model-authored copy through JSON/Python escaping.\nPaper workflow:\n1. Plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json; call read_pdf ONCE for the task's full page range.\nThis extracts to local storage and logs read_pdf.py; only bounded batches reach the model. Do not print all pages.\n2. Read the delivered page batches in order. Record a topic's supported findings as soon as useful; do not\nwait until both questions are answered. The next batch follows successful actions automatically. On an\naction error, correct it using the retained batch. Do not call read_pdf/task_status just to advance.\nUse only evidence ids from delivered Evidence headers.\n3. Update the same topic note incrementally, preserving earlier confirmed facts and citations. Each final\ntopic note must contain its two answers, PDF page numbers and continuous exact quotations supporting ALL\nanswer items, within 1500 characters.\nUse write_note(title=..., content=..., evidence_ids=['ev-...'], section='overview') with the actual topic.\n4. After full coverage, reuse all five final notes, build report.json across actions if needed, test, finish plan.\nThis agent already has versioned evidence, bounded page selection, note reuse, tools and verification.\nMulti-agent collaboration and training are future suggestions, not implemented features.\n\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"read\",\"next_requirement\":\"PDF pages not yet sent: 2\",\"remaining_count\":7,\"requests_left\":1,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":0,\"request_number\":2,\"max_requests\":3,\"requests_after_response\":1,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"full_reads_registered\":{\"report.json\":\"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\"},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"pdf_pages_missing\":[2]}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"thought\": \"Execute the next action.\", \"code\": \"print('Read initial page one.')\"}"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\nRead initial page one.\nLas